'''Terraspin''' is the [[Omnitrix]]'s DNA sample of a [[Geochelone Aerios]]<ref>[[Khyber]]</ref><ref>''[[Of Predators and Prey: Part 2]]</ref>{{Refn|group = note|The page for Terraspin's species was originally created under the title "Geochelone Aerios" on August 25, 2010, which was the name featured in Terraspin's Alien Data File as both the singular and plural forms of the species.{{Refn|Issue #58; [[:File:Aldabra Lore.png|file]]|group=AP|name = image}} The page was renamed to "Geochelone Aerio" a day later on August 26, 2010 by [[User:Linkmadara|Linkmadara]], with the name being used as the species' singular form on the wiki until February 16, 2024, when it was discovered that "Geochelone Aerios" was used for both the singular and plural forms of the species as evidenced by the Data File and the closed captions for ''[[Of Predators and Prey: Part 2]]''.{{Refn|[[:File:Geochelone Aerios Official Spelling from Subtitles.png]]|group = captions|name = subtitles}}{{Refn|www.cartoonnetwork.com|group = CN}} In that time, Terraspin's species was listed as "Geochelone Areio", a misspelling of "Geochelone Aerio", in the Alien Database on the ''[[Ben 10 Omniverse: Aliens at War]]'' DVD.{{Refn|''[[Ben 10 Omniverse: Aliens at War]]''; [[:File:OV AAW DVD Terraspin Data.png|file]]|group = DVD}}{{Refn|[[Ben 10 Planet:Longstanding Misinformation]]|group = BTP|name = misinfo}}}} from the planet [[Aldabra]]<ref>[[Galapagus]]</ref><ref name="EfA">''[[Escape From Aggregor]]''</ref> in the [[Andromeda (Classic)|Andromeda Galaxy]].

==Appearance==
Terraspin is a green [[Wikipedia:Turtle|turtle]]-like alien with large flipper-like arms, green eyes, and stumpy legs. The tips of his arms also have three holes each, which can extend finger-like claws to use as fingers.

In '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]''', Terraspin had eight holes in his shell and a circular body shape.

In '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''', Terraspin looks mostly the same, except he now has six holes in his shell, brown spots on his upper legs, toes, and shoulders, and a hexagonal and slightly larger body shape. The black stripes under his eyes are thicker, his legs are shorter, and his feet have each gained three toes.

Terraspin wears the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]]/[[Omnitrix (Omniverse)|Omnitrix]] symbol on his chest.

==Powers and Abilities==
<gallery type="slideshow">
CF (406).png|Fan Blade Formation/Aerokinetic Blasts
I13 (75).png|Aerokinetic Redirection
The More Things Change, Part 2 (287).png|Aerokinetic Suction/Air Absorption
SS (189).png|Tornado Generation
MHR (345).png|Sharp Fan Blades
MHR (337).png|Flight/Enhanced Speed
TUH (462).png|Levitation
RotS (81).png|Enhanced Strength
MHR (338).png|Enhanced Durability
The More Things Change, Part 2 (284).png|Poisonous Gas Immunity
TFoC (61).png|Retractable Head/Retractable Limbs
</gallery>
From the vents on his front shell, Terraspin can expel powerful gusts of wind to push opponents away.<ref name="UA">''[[Ultimate Aggregor (Episode)|Ultimate Aggregor]]''</ref> He can also form his limbs into rotating fans to amplify this; where his fins become triangular and sharp,<ref name="MHR">''[[Many Happy Returns]]''</ref> and his legs combine and morph into a similar shape. In combination, Terraspin's three fans can whirl incredibly fast, while his shell stays static and suspended in the air, and generate hurricane-force winds<ref name="EfA" /> or destructive, mini corkscrew cyclones.<ref>''[[Simian Says]]''</ref><ref name="TFOC">''[[The Forge of Creation]]''</ref>{{Refn|group = AP|name = image}} Terraspin also possesses aerokinesis,{{Refn|''[[Ben 10 Ultimate Alien: Escape From Aggregor]]''; [[:File:EFA DVD Terraspin Data.png|file]]|group = DVD|name = DVD}} allowing him to influence the direction of wind in the air,<ref name="EfA" /> and generate tornadoes without spinning, as demonstrated by [[Ultimate Kevin]].<ref>''[[Absolute Power: Part 2]]''</ref>

Terraspin's wind blasts are powerful enough to put out fires<ref>''[[Basic Training]]''</ref> and redirect objects.<ref>''[[Inspector 13]]''</ref>{{Refn|[[:File:Terraspin Can Redirect Solid Objects.png]]|group = DM}} Terraspin can also harness his aerokinetic powers to fly, blowing air to hover over a surface and using his rotating limbs as propellers.{{Refn|group = DVD|name = DVD}}

Terraspin can also spin in reverse, creating strong vacuums.<ref name="TUH">''[[The Ultimate Heist]]''</ref> Terraspin can utilize this to absorb lethal toxins out of the nearby air.<ref name="TMTCP2">''[[The More Things Change: Part 2]]''</ref>

Terraspin possesses enhanced strength, as he was able to hold a giant robot with his bare hands while spinning<ref name="RG">''[[Reflected Glory]]''</ref> and charge into a building by busting down a door.<ref name="RotS">''[[Revenge of the Swarm]]''</ref>

Terraspin possesses enhanced durability, as his thick, impermeable shell protects him from most assaults.{{Refn|group = AP|name = image}}<ref name="EfA" /><ref name="MHR" />

Terraspin is immune to poisonous gas.<ref name="TMTCP2" /> He is also resistant to [[manna]], as demonstrated by [[Ultimate Aggregor]].<ref>''[[Map of Infinity (Episode)|Map of Infinity]]''</ref>

Terraspin can extend the black holes at the tips of his flippers into finger-like claws, as demonstrated by Galapagus.<ref name="EfA" /> Terraspin can also fully retract his head and limbs into his shell.<ref name="TFOC" />

Terraspin is capable of using [[Magic (Classic)|magic]],{{Refn|[[:File:Geochelone Aerios Could Learn Magic.PNG]]|group = DM}} as demonstrated by [[Addwaitya]].<ref name="WTMH">''[[Where the Magic Happens]]''</ref> <ref>''[[Enemy of My Frenemy]]''</ref> However, Ben cannot stay transformed as Terraspin long enough to learn it without Master Control.{{Refn|[[:File:Terraspin and Snare-Oh Cannot Learn Magic.png]]|group = DJW}}

==Weaknesses ==
[[File:Terraspin Jammed.png|thumb|218x218px|Jammed Air Vents]]
Unless he is flying, Terraspin's body is cumbersome and not very agile, as [[Attea]] claims if he wanted to run, [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] picked the wrong species to turn into.<ref>''[[Vilgax Must Croak]]''</ref>

When Terraspin is spinning around, the air vents on his chest are vulnerable to being jammed with large foreign objects. This causes him immense discomfort and forces him to stop spinning and remove the object.<ref name="TUH" />

Terraspin is not fully immune to manna attacks, as demonstrated by [[Galapagus]].<ref name="EfA" /><ref name="UA" />

As demonstrated with Addwaitya, Terraspin is vulnerable to electricity, such as that generated by an [[Amperi (Classic)|Amperi]].<ref name="WTMH" />

==History ==
===Ultimate Alien===  
*In ''[[Escape From Aggregor]]'', Terraspin's DNA was sampled and put in the [[Codon Stream]] when the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]] scanned [[Galapagus]]' DNA.﻿
*Terraspin first appeared in ''[[Reflected Glory]]'', where he fought and destroyed a giant robot created by the [[Forever Knights]].
*In ''[[The Forge of Creation]]'', Terraspin defeated some [[Aggrebot]]s in the [[Rustbucket 3]].
*In ''[[Absolute Power: Part 1]]'', Terraspin blew [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] into a wall, but she used a [[Spells (Classic)|spell]] to slow him down, making him powerless and forcing him to switch into [[NRG]].
*In ''[[Revenge of the Swarm]]'', Terraspin, Gwen, and [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] broke into [[Dr. Victor Valadis|Victor]]'s old lab and met the [[Valadis Laboratories Janitor|janitor]].
*In ''[[Basic Training]]'', Terraspin put out a fire in [[Hulka]]'s barracks.
*In ''[[Simian Says]]'', Terraspin briefly battled some [[DNAlien]] [[Arachnachimp (Classic)|Arachnachimp]]s until he reverted.
*In ''[[The Widening Gyre]]'', Terraspin fought some [[Mutant Seagull (The Widening Gyre)|mutated seagulls]].
*In ''[[Inspector 13]]'', Terraspin blew all of [[Thirteen]]'s bombs away to get [[Julie Yamamoto|Julie]] to safety.

===Omniverse===
*In ''[[The More Things Change: Part 2]]'', Terraspin sucked all the gas out of an [[Undertown]] establishment named [[Gas House]], revealing [[Bubble Helmet]], who falls to the ground because he can't breathe. After [[Rook Blonko|Rook]] accidentally let him get away, he chased him with Rook on top until he was cornered by [[Psyphon's Gang|Psyphon's gang]].
*In ''[[Many Happy Returns]]'', Terraspin was defeated by [[Looma Red Wind|Princess Looma]].
*In ''[[T.G.I.S.]]'', Terraspin battled some [[Chupacabra]]s.
*In ''[[Vilgax Must Croak]]'', Terraspin blew away [[Attea|General Attea]] and [[EightEight]].
*In ''[[While You Were Away]]'', Terraspin helped land the [[Rook Ben's Harvester|harvester ship]] [[Rook Ben|Young One]] was piloting.
*In ''[[The Ultimate Heist]]'', Terraspin battled [[Albedo|Negative]] [[Goop (Classic)|Goop]] and tried to get the [[Polymorphic Crystal]], but failed when [[Albedo]] threw an object that jammed his shell.
*In ''[[For a Few Brains More]]'', Terraspin rescued [[Azmuth (Classic)|Azmuth]] and his brain.
*In ''[[Catfight]]'', Terraspin battled Princess Looma until Attea used the [[Omnitrix Remote Control]] to change him into [[Bullfrag]].
*In ''[[Universe vs. Tennyson]]'', Terraspin defeated [[Fistina]].
*In ''[[Rook Tales]]'', Terraspin failed to take off Young One's tail.
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Terraspin appeared for a short time when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was cycling through his aliens.

