==Etymology==
Terraspin's name is a portmanteau of [[Wikipedia:Terrapin|terrapin]], which is a turtle or [[Wikipedia:Tortoise|tortoise]], as well as "spin," which alludes to his ability to do so.

==Trivia==
*Whenever Terraspin talks in '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''', a fan sound is played in the background.
*Terraspin and the other [[Andromeda (Classic)|Andromeda]] aliens have their powers related to a certain element; for Terraspin, it is wind.
*Terraspin was the [[Alien of the Month]] in March 2011.
*Terraspin resembles, and looks roughly similar to, the Japanese monster [[Wikipedia:Gamera|Gamera]]; both of them are turtle-like in appearance and can draw into their shells and spin as either an attack or a form of flight.
*Terraspin did not appear in ''[[Where the Magic Happens]]'' because Ben simply did not know said transformation would have been particularly useful in the magical environment of [[Legerdomain]] at the time.{{Refn|[[:File:Why Terraspin Was Not Used in WTMH.PNG]]|group = DM}}
*Terraspin went through many name changes during development, but the early names were all shut down by the writer's legal team.{{Refn|[[:File:Kathleen David Named Terraspin.png]]|group = PAD|name = link 1}}
**Eventually, however, Terraspin was named by Kathleen David, the wife of writer [[Peter David]].{{Refn|group = PAD|name = link 1}}
*Terraspin was originally not supposed to appear in:
**''[[Revenge of the Swarm]]'', with his role taken by [[Diamondhead (Classic)|Diamondhead]].{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/8/84/Revenge_of_the_Swarm_DRAFT-1.pdf ''Revenge of the Swarm'' Script First Draft]|group = script|name = first}}
**''[[Basic Training]]'', with his role taken by [[Waterhazard]].{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/3/31/Basic_Training_Draft-1.pdf ''Basic Training'' Script First Draft]|group = script|name = script}}
*Terraspin was designed by [[Steven Choi]] or [[Chap Yaep]].{{Refn|[[:File:Steven and Chap Andromeda.png]]|group = DJW}}
*[[Ben 23]] has an alternate counterpart of Terraspin.{{Refn|[[:File:Ben 23 Andromeda Aliens.png]]|group = DJW}}
*When designing a version of [[Shellhead (Thomas Perkins)|Shellhead]] in 2020, [[Thomas N. Perkins IV]] felt like doing something different for Shellhead, believing that the franchise did not need another turtle-based alien like Terraspin.{{Refn|[[:File:Shellhead Not Turtle Reason.png]]|group = TNP}}{{Refn|[[:File:Shellhead Not Turtle Reason 2.png]]|group = TNP}}

